<title>USA: U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended Aug 30, compared with the Aug 23 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.21 vs 5.18</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.09 vs 5.02</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.43 vs 5.40</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.33 vs 5.29</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.42 vs 5.37</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.40 vs 5.38</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............7.03 vs 6.84</p>
</text>
